    {
      "id": "s1",
      "type": "info",
      "text": "**Alt key tips** let you control the ribbon with your keyboard. Pressing `Alt` displays letter badges over the ribbon tabs (`H` is the Home tab). Press each letter in order, one at a time. Mac Excel does not support ribbon key tips, so Mac learners can skip the keyboard steps in this lesson."
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "type": "select",
      "prompt": "A bakery tracks its daily bake. Select the header in `A1` that you will format: `A1`.",
      "grid": [
        [
          "Item",
          "Category",
          "Trays",
          "Status"
        ],
        [
          "Sourdough Loaf",
          "Bread",
          12,
          "Ready"
        ],
